{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012DVXyze4c2epnoyULEgtnQ","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Commentary Talent CRM — Implementation Plan\n     2→\n     3→**PRD:** PRD-Commentary-Talent-CRM-2026-03-10.md\n     4→\n     5→> **Phase 1 (Talent Roster UI) is already complete.** This plan covers Phases 0, 2, 3, 4, 5.\n     6→\n     7→---\n     8→\n     9→## Phases Overview\n    10→\n    11→| Phase | Description | Tasks | Status |\n    12→|-------|-------------|-------|--------|\n    13→| Phase 0 | Data Migration Script | 1 | COMPLETE |\n    14→| Phase 0-Deploy | Run migration + verify Firebase | 1 | NOT STARTED |\n    15→| Phase 2 | Booking Links + Smart Availability | 6 | NOT STARTED |\n    16→| Phase 2-Deploy | Deploy Phase 2 changes | 1 | NOT STARTED |\n    17→| Phase 3 | Gmail + Google Calendar Outreach | 5 | NOT STARTED |\n    18→| Phase 3-Deploy | Deploy Phase 3 changes | 1 | NOT STARTED |\n    19→| Phase 4 | AI-Powered Talent Discovery | 5 | NOT STARTED |\n    20→| Phase 4-Deploy | Deploy Phase 4 changes | 1 | NOT STARTED |\n    21→| Phase 5 | Annual Survey + Pre-Production Alerts | 6 | NOT STARTED |\n    22→| Phase 5-Deploy | Deploy Phase 5 changes | 1 | NOT STARTED |\n    23→| Final-Deploy | Full acceptance criteria check | 2 | NOT STARTED |\n    24→| **Total** | | **30** | |\n    25→\n    26→---\n    27→\n    28→## Phase 0: Data Migration Script\n    29→\n    30→> **Deploy rule:** This is a server-side script, not a frontend build. The deploy task runs the script\n    31→> directly (no npm build needed). Firebase-only changes.\n    32→\n    33→### Task 0.1: Create CSV migration script — COMPLETE\n    34→\n    35→**File:** `server/scripts/migrateCommentaryCSV.js` (new file)\n    36→\n    37→**Change:** Create a Node.js script with the following behavior:\n    38→\n    39→```javascript\n    40→// Usage: node server/scripts/migrateCommentaryCSV.js [--dry-run]\n    41→//\n    42→// Reads 3 CSVs:\n    43→//   docs/PRD-Commentary-Talent-CRM/Master 2026_ Commentary Tracker - Commentators 2026.csv\n    44→//   docs/PRD-Commentary-Talent-CRM/Master 2026_ Commentary Tracker - 2026 Assignment.csv\n    45→//   docs/PRD-Commentary-Talent-CRM/Official Virtius Remote Commentary 2026 (Responses) - Form Responses 1 (6).csv\n    46→//\n    47→// Writes to Firebase: talentRoster/{talentId}\n    48→// Status mapping: \"Ready\" → \"ready\", \"Did 2025\" → \"did-2025\", \"Need Info\" → \"need-info\", \"Has Contact\" → \"has-contact\"\n    49→// Role mapping: \"Play by Play / Lead\" → \"pbp\", \"Color / Analyst\" → \"analyst\", \"Does not matter\" → \"both\"\n    50→// Dry-run: prints summary, no writes\n    51→// Flags: malformed phone/email, fuzzy duplicate names (>90% Levenshtein similarity)\n    52→// Outputs log: server/scripts/migration-log.json\n    53→// Summary line: \"X created, Y enriched (survey), Z assignments added, N flagged\"\n    54→```\n    55→\n    56→**Firebase Admin initialization (required in script):**\n    57→```javascript\n    58→const path = require('path');\n    59→const admin = require('firebase-admin');\n    60→// Must run with GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS set (same as coordinator server)\n    61→admin.initializeApp({ credential: admin.credential.applicationDefault() });\n    62→const db = admin.database();\n    63→```\n    64→\n    65→**CSV path resolution:** Use `path.resolve(__dirname, '../../', 'docs/PRD-Commentary-Talent-CRM/...')` — paths are relative to the script file, not `process.cwd()`.\n    66→\n    67→**talentId format:** Generate as sanitized lowercase-dashed name: `name.toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/g, '-')`. If a collision is detected (same key, different email), append `-2`, `-3` etc. This format is consistent with how other roster entries reference talent across phases.\n    68→\n    69→**Idempotency:** Before writing each record, check `talentRoster/{talentId}`. If it exists (match by email), UPDATE (merge) rather than overwrite. Log \"enriched\" for updates, \"created\" for new records.\n    70→\n    71→**compId mapping for history:** The assignment CSV has meet names/dates, not Firebase push-key IDs. There is no lookup table. Write `competitionHistory` using the raw meet name as a placeholder compId (e.g., `\"2025-01-18-stanford-vs-cal\"`). This data is informational; the `compId` field is best-effort and will not link to live Firebase competition records.\n    72→\n    73→Use `csv-parse` for CSV parsing (install if not present). Use a simple Levenshtein function for duplicate detection.\n    74→\n    75→**Schema written to Firebase:**\n    76→```json\n    77→{\n    78→  \"name\": \"First Last\",\n    79→  \"phone\": \"+1...\",\n    80→  \"email\": \"...\",\n    81→  \"wagMag\": \"WAG | MAG | Both\",\n    82→  \"commentaryRole\": \"pbp | analyst | both\",\n    83→  \"status\": \"ready | has-contact | did-2025 | need-info\",\n    84→  \"affiliation\": \"...\",\n    85→  \"conference\": \"...\",\n    86→  \"canProduce\": true,\n    87→  \"notes\": \"...\",\n    88→  \"competitionHistory\": [{ \"compId\": \"...\", \"role\": \"pbp\", \"date\": \"...\" }],\n    89→  \"surveyCompleted\": true,\n    90→  \"textSent\": true,\n    91→  \"discordAdded\": false,\n    92→  \"internetUploadMbps\": 50,\n    93→  \"internetDownloadMbps\": 100,\n    94→  \"createdAt\": \"ISO timestamp\",\n    95→  \"updatedAt\": \"ISO timestamp\"\n    96→}\n    97→```\n    98→\n    99→**Implements:** Phase 0 acceptance criteria (dry-run, 428 contacts, survey enrichment, assignments, flagging)\n   100→\n   101→---\n   102→\n   103→## Phase 0-Deploy: Run Migration + Verify\n   104→\n   105→> **This is a deploy/run task.** No build needed — just run the script and verify Firebase.\n   106→\n   107→### Task 0-D.1: Run migration and verify data in Firebase — NOT STARTED\n   108→\n   109→**Steps:**\n   110→1. Create screenshots directory: `mkdir -p docs/PRD-Commentary-Talent-CRM/screenshots`\n   111→2. Dry-run first: `GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS=/opt/gymnastics-graphics/firebase-service-account.json node server/scripts/migrateCommentaryCSV.js --dry-run`\n   112→3. Review output — confirm counts look correct (expect ~428 contacts)\n   113→4. Live run: `GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS=/opt/gymnastics-graphics/firebase-service-account.json node server/scripts/migrateCommentaryCSV.js`\n   114→5. Navigate to `https://commentarygraphic.com/talent` with Playwright\n   115→6. Take screenshot → `docs/PRD-Commentary-Talent-CRM/screenshots/verify-phase0-talent-list.png`\n   116→7. Verify talent count shown matches expected (~428)\n   117→\n   118→**Checks:**\n   119→- [ ] No crash during dry-run\n   120→- [ ] Live run creates records in Firebase `talentRoster/`\n   121→- [ ] Talent page shows records (not empty)\n   122→- [ ] migration-log.json exists and lists flagged rows\n   123→\n   124→---\n   125→\n   126→## Phase 2: Booking Links + Smart Availability\n   127→\n   128→> **Deploy rule:** Commit each task. Do NOT deploy until Phase 2-Deploy.\n   129→> **Prerequisite:** `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` must be set in server `.env` on `44.193.31.120` (used by Task 2.4 note parsing endpoint).\n   130→\n   131→### Task 2.1: Add booking token server endpoints — NOT STARTED\n   132→\n   133→**File:** `server/index.js`\n   134→\n   135→**Architecture note:** `BookingPage` is a public page accessed by talent (no login, no session). The coordinator server (`44.193.31.120:3003`) has an auto-shutdown feature and may be offline when a talent clicks a link 2 weeks later. The frontend has no established pattern for calling the coordinator directly from the browser.\n   136→\n   137→**Solution: BookingPage reads/writes Firebase directly, not via coordinator.** Only the token generation endpoint (called by the authenticated coordinator UI) goes through the coordinator server. All public-facing operations use Firebase with appropriate security rules.\n   138→\n   139→```javascript\n   140→// POST /api/book/generate — creates a booking token (coordinator-side, auth required)\n   141→// Body: { talentId, compId, role }\n   142→// Writes: bookingTokens/{uuid} = { talentId, compId, role, createdAt, expiresAt (30 days from now, ISO), responded: false }\n   143→// Also updates: competitions/{compId}/commentary/{talentId}.status = 'invited', invitedAt = now\n   144→// Returns: { token, url: `https://commentarygraphic.com/book/${uuid}` }\n   145→```\n   146→\n   147→**Public-facing (BookingPage reads Firebase directly, no coordinator):**\n   148→```javascript\n   149→// BookingPage reads these Firebase paths directly:\n   150→//   bookingTokens/{token}          → token metadata (talentId, compId, role, expiresAt, responded)\n   151→//   competitions/{compId}/config   → { eventName, meetDate, venue }\n   152→//   talentRoster/{talentId}        → { name }\n   153→//\n   154→// BookingPage writes these Firebase paths directly:\n   155→//   On \"Yes\":\n   156→//     competitions/{compId}/commentary/{talentId}: { status: 'confirmed', confirmedAt: now }\n   157→//     bookingTokens/{token}: { responded: true, response: 'yes' }\n   158→//\n   159→//   On \"No\" (save interested comps):\n   160→//     For each selected compId: talentRoster/{talentId}/interested/{compId} = true\n   161→//     (keyed object, not array — avoids overwriting previous interests)\n   162→//     bookingTokens/{token}: { responded: true, response: 'no' }\n   163→//\n   164→// BookingPage fetches upcoming competitions from Firebase:\n   165→//   competitions/ — filter by config.meetDate > now, exclude original compId\n   166→//   Show next 5 sorted by meetDate asc\n   167→//\n   168→// Expiry + double-response guards (client-side):\n   169→//   If token.expiresAt < now → show \"This link has expired\"\n   170→//   If token.responded === true → show \"You've already responded\"\n   171→```\n   172→\n   173→**Firebase security rules update required** (in `database.rules.json`):\n   174→```json\n   175→\"bookingTokens\": {\n   176→  \"$token\": {\n   177→    \".read\": true,\n   178→    \".write\": \"auth == null || auth != null\"\n   179→  }\n   180→}\n   181→```\n   182→(public read of token; public write to `responded` and `response` fields — scope carefully)\n   183→\n   184→**Implements:** Booking token generation, Yes/No response flow\n   185→\n   186→---\n   187→\n   188→### Task 2.2: Create public BookingPage — NOT STARTED\n   189→\n   190→**File:** `show-controller/src/pages/BookingPage.jsx` (new file)\n   191→\n   192→**Change:** Create a public page (no auth required) that reads/writes Firebase directly (NOT the coordinator server — see Task 2.1 architecture note):\n   193→- Imports `{ db, ref, get, update, set }` from `../lib/firebase`\n   194→- Reads `bookingTokens/{token}`, `competitions/{compId}/config`, `talentRoster/{talentId}` on load\n   195→- Guards: if token expired → \"This link has expired\"; if already responded → \"You've already responded\"\n   196→- Shows: competition eventName, meetDate, venue, talent's name, assigned role\n   197→- Has two primary buttons: \"Yes, I'm available\" and \"No, not this one\"\n   198→- On \"Yes\": writes to Firebase directly (see Task 2.1), shows confirmation screen\n   199→- On \"No\": queries `competitions/` from Firebase, filters meetDate > now, shows next 5 as checkboxes; submit writes `talentRoster/{talentId}/interested/{compId} = true` for each checked\n   200→- Mobile-first layout (talent opens this on their phone)\n   201→- No navbar, no auth, standalone page with minimal styling\n   202→\n   203→Reference `../lib/firebase` import pattern from `useCommentaryStaff.js`.\n   204→\n   205→**Implements:** Public booking response flow\n   206→\n   207→---\n   208→\n   209→### Task 2.3: Add public route for booking page — NOT STARTED\n   210→\n   211→**File:** `show-controller/src/App.jsx`\n   212→\n   213→**Change:** Add `/book/:token` route that renders BookingPage without auth guard:\n   214→\n   215→```jsx\n   216→// CRITICAL: Place BEFORE the <Route path=\"/:compId\"> wildcard (App.jsx line ~101)\n   217→// or the router will treat \"book\" as a competition ID.\n   218→// App.jsx has no global auth wrapper — just insert before the /:compId route.\n   219→<Route path=\"/book/:token\" element={<BookingPage />} />\n   220→```\n   221→\n   222→There is no global auth wrapper in App.jsx (only `<CoordinatorGate>` wraps `/_admin/vm-pool`).\n   223→The route must be placed before `<Route path=\"/:compId\" element={<CompetitionLayout />}>`.\n   224→Read App.jsx first to confirm placement.\n   225→\n   226→**Implements:** Public access to booking page\n   227→\n   228→---\n   229→\n   230→### Task 2.4: Add note parsing endpoint — NOT STARTED\n   231→\n   232→**File:** `server/index.js`\n   233→\n   234→**Change:** Add a new endpoint that calls Claude API to extract date hints from talent notes:\n   235→\n   236→```javascript\n   237→// POST /api/talent/:talentId/notes/parse\n   238→// Body: { noteText: \"She's available late February but busy Jan 15\" }\n   239→// Calls Claude API (claude-haiku-4-5-20251001) with prompt:\n   240→//   \"Extract any date mentions or availability hints from this note.\n   241→//    Return JSON: { availablePeriods: ['late February'], unavailableDates: ['January 15'] }\"\n   242→// Writes parsed hints to talentRoster/{talentId}.parsedAvailability = { ... }\n   243→// Returns: { availablePeriods, unavailableDates }\n   244→```\n   245→\n   246→Requires `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` in server `.env`. Use the `@anthropic-ai/sdk` package.\n   247→\n   248→**Implements:** AI note parsing for availability tracking\n   249→\n   250→---\n   251→\n   252→### Task 2.5: Add \"Interested\" badge + note parsing trigger to TalentProfilePage — NOT STARTED\n   253→\n   254→**File:** `show-controller/src/pages/TalentProfilePage.jsx`\n   255→\n   256→**Change:**\n   257→1. When a note is saved (existing \"Save Notes\" button), also call `POST /api/talent/:talentId/notes/parse` with the note text\n   258→2. Show any parsed availability periods as small tags below the notes field: `Available: late February` (green), `Busy: January 15` (red)\n   259→3. These tags are read from `talent.parsedAvailability.availablePeriods` and `unavailableDates`\n   260→\n   261→**Implements:** Visual feedback for AI-parsed availability\n   262→\n   263→---\n   264→\n   265→### Task 2.6: Add booking link generation + Interested badge to CommentaryPage — NOT STARTED\n   266→\n   267→**File:** `show-controller/src/pages/CommentaryPage.jsx`\n   268→\n   269→**Change:**\n   270→1. Next to each assigned talent in the assignments list, add a small \"🔗 Copy Link\" button\n   271→2. Clicking \"🔗 Copy Link\" calls `POST /api/book/generate` with `{ talentId, compId, role }`, then copies the returned URL to clipboard\n   272→3. Show a small \"Copied!\" toast for 2 seconds\n   273→4. In the talent search panel (right side), show an \"Interested\" badge (green pill: \"Interested ✓\") next to any talent whose `talentRoster/{id}.interested` array contains the current `compId`\n   274→\n   275→**Implements:** Booking link generation, interested badge in assignment panel\n   276→\n   277→---\n   278→\n   279→## Phase 2-Deploy: Deploy Phase 2 Changes\n   280→\n   281→> **This is a deploy task.** Build frontend + deploy coordinator server changes.\n   282→\n   283→### Task 2-D.1: Build, deploy, and verify Phase 2 — NOT STARTED\n   284→\n   285→**Frontend changed?** Yes (`BookingPage.jsx`, `App.jsx`, `CommentaryPage.jsx`, `TalentProfilePage.jsx`)\n   286→```bash\n   287→cd show-controller && npm run build\n   288→# then upload dist per CLAUDE.md Step 1\n   289→```\n   290→\n   291→**Server changed?** Yes (`server/index.js` — new endpoints)\n   292→```bash\n   293→# SSH to coordinator (44.193.31.120)\n   294→# cd /opt/gymnastics-graphics\n   295→# git pull origin main\n   296→# pm2 restart coordinator (with GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS per CLAUDE.md)\n   297→```\n   298→\n   299→**Verify:**\n   300→- [ ] Navigate to `/talent` — no console errors\n   301→- [ ] Open a competition's commentary page — \"🔗 Copy Link\" button appears next to assignments\n   302→- [ ] Navigate to `/book/test-token-invalid` — BookingPage loads (may show error for invalid token, but page renders)\n   303→- [ ] Take screenshot → `docs/PRD-Commentary-Talent-CRM/screenshots/verify-phase2-booking-link.png`\n   304→\n   305→---\n   306→\n   307→## Phase 3: Gmail + Google Calendar Outreach\n   308→\n   309→> **Deploy rule:** Commit each task. Do NOT deploy until Phase 3-Deploy.\n   310→> **Prerequisite:** `GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID`, `GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET`, `GOOGLE_REFRESH_TOKEN` must be set in server `.env` on `44.193.31.120`.\n   311→\n   312→### Task 3.1: Create Gmail service — NOT STARTED\n   313→\n   314→**File:** `server/lib/gmailService.js` (new file)\n   315→\n   316→**Change:** Create a Gmail OAuth service using `googleapis` npm package:\n   317→\n   318→```javascript\n   319→// gmailService.js exports:\n   320→// sendEmail({ to, subject, html }) — sends via coordinator's Gmail account\n   321→// Uses OAuth2 with GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID, GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET, GOOGLE_REFRESH_TOKEN from process.env\n   322→// Returns message ID on success, throws on failure\n   323→\n   324→// Email templates (inline):\n   325→// - inviteEmail(talent, competition, role, bookingUrl) → HTML invite with event details + booking link\n   326→//   NOTE: bookingUrl is required — the invite endpoint (Task 3.3) must generate the token FIRST\n   327→// - briefingEmail(talent, competition, virtiusUrl, discordInfo, preProdTime) → HTML briefing\n   328→// - reminderEmail(talent, competition, bookingUrl) → HTML reminder with booking link\n   329→```\n   330→\n   331→Install `googleapis` if not already in `server/package.json`.\n   332→\n   333→**Implements:** Gmail outreach capability\n   334→\n   335→---\n   336→\n   337→### Task 3.2: Create Google Calendar service — NOT STARTED\n   338→\n   339→**File:** `server/lib/googleCalendarService.js` (new file)\n   340→\n   341→**Change:** Create a GCal service using `googleapis`:\n   342→\n   343→```javascript\n   344→// googleCalendarService.js exports:\n   345→// createCompetitionEvent({ talentEmail, competitionName, startTime, discordInfo })\n   346→//   → Creates GCal event 1 hour before startTime, adds talent as attendee\n   347→//   → Returns eventId\n   348→//\n   349→// createPreProdMeeting({ talentEmail, meetingTime, competitionName })\n   350→//   → Creates GCal event at meetingTime\n   351→//   → Returns eventId\n   352→```\n   353→\n   354→**Implements:** Calendar invite capability\n   355→\n   356→---\n   357→\n   358→### Task 3.3: Add outreach API endpoints — NOT STARTED\n   359→\n   360→**File:** `server/index.js`\n   361→\n   362→**Change:** Add outreach endpoints (import gmailService and googleCalendarService at top):\n   363→\n   364→```javascript\n   365→// POST /api/commentary/:compId/:talentId/invite\n   366→//   Step 1: Generate a booking token (reuse Task 2.1 token generation logic)\n   367→//           bookingTokens/{uuid} = { talentId, compId, role, ... }\n   368→//           bookingUrl = `https://commentarygraphic.com/book/${uuid}`\n   369→//   Step 2: Send invite email via gmailService.sendEmail(inviteEmail(talent, competition, role, bookingUrl))\n   370→//   Step 3: Update competitions/{compId}/commentary/{talentId}: { status: 'invited', invitedAt: now }\n   371→//   Step 4: Append to communicationLog (see log shape below)\n   372→\n   373→// POST /api/commentary/:compId/:talentId/briefing\n   374→//   Body: { virtiusUrl: string, discordInfo: string, preProdTime: ISO string }\n   375→//   All three fields are required — return 400 if any are missing\n   376→//   Sends briefing email, updates .briefedAt = now, status = 'briefed'\n   377→//   Appends to communicationLog\n   378→\n   379→// POST /api/commentary/:compId/:talentId/calendar-invite\n   380→//   Creates GCal event 1 hour before competition start (read meetDate from competitions/{compId}/config)\n   381→//   Updates .calendarInviteSent = true\n   382→//   Appends to communicationLog\n   383→\n   384→// POST /api/commentary/:compId/:talentId/schedule-preproduction\n   385→//   Body: { meetingTime: ISO string }\n   386→//   Creates pre-prod GCal event, adds talent as attendee\n   387→//   Updates .preProductionMeetingScheduled = meetingTime\n   388→//   Appends to communicationLog\n   389→\n   390→// communicationLog — use Firebase push keys, NOT an array:\n   391→//   talentRoster/{talentId}/communicationLog/{pushKey} = { type, sentAt, note }\n   392→//   Firebase RTDB has no arrayUnion — push keys avoid read-then-write race conditions\n   393→// Log entry shape: { type: 'invite'|'briefing'|'calendar'|'preproduction'|'imessage', sentAt: ISO, note: '...' }\n   394→```\n   395→\n   396→**Implements:** All outreach server actions\n   397→\n   398→---\n   399→\n   400→### Task 3.4: Add outreach buttons to CommentaryPage — NOT STARTED\n   401→\n   402→**File:** `show-controller/src/pages/CommentaryPage.jsx`\n   403→\n   404→**Change:** In the assignment detail view (when a talent card is expanded/selected):\n   405→1. Add outreach action buttons: \"Send Invite\", \"Send Briefing\", \"Calendar Invite\", \"Schedule Pre-Prod\"\n   406→2. \"Send Invite\" calls endpoint directly (endpoint generates token internally — no extra input needed)\n   407→3. \"Send Briefing\" must open a small modal first to collect 3 required fields:\n   408→   - Virtius session URL (text input)\n   409→   - Discord info (text input, e.g. room name/link)\n   410→   - Pre-production meeting time (datetime-local input)\n   411→   Only after the coordinator fills these and clicks \"Send\" does the modal call the briefing endpoint.\n   412→   Without this modal, the briefing endpoint has no data to put in the email.\n   413→4. \"Schedule Pre-Prod\" opens a datetime picker modal; submits `{ meetingTime }` to endpoint\n   414→5. Each button has a sibling \"📋 Copy for iMessage\" button that:\n   415→   - Formats the same message as the email (plain text)\n   416→   - Copies to clipboard\n   417→   - Shows: \"Sent via iMessage?\" → [Yes] → logs `{ type: 'imessage', sentAt: now }` to server\n   418→6. Show a \"Sent ✓\" indicator when the server confirms the email was sent\n   419→\n   420→**Implements:** Coordinator-facing outreach UI\n   421→\n   422→---\n   423→\n   424→### Task 3.5: Add screenshot upload + communications tab to TalentProfilePage — NOT STARTED\n   425→\n   426→**File:** `show-controller/src/pages/TalentProfilePage.jsx`\n   427→\n   428→**Change:**\n   429→1. Add a \"Communications\" tab alongside the existing profile sections\n   430→2. Communications tab shows `talent.communicationLog` entries sorted by `sentAt` desc, showing type + timestamp + note\n   431→3. Add a \"Upload Screenshot\" button — accepts image file, converts to base64, sends to a new endpoint `POST /api/talent/:talentId/parse-screenshot` which calls Claude API vision to extract availability text from the screenshot\n   432→4. Extracted text appears as a new note with prefix `[From screenshot] ` and triggers note parsing\n   433→\n   434→Add new server endpoint:\n   435→```javascript\n   436→// POST /api/talent/:talentId/parse-screenshot\n   437→// Body: { imageBase64, mimeType }\n   438→// Calls Claude API with image, extracts availability mentions\n   439→// Returns: { extractedText, availablePeriods, unavailableDates }\n   440→// Writes extracted note to talent's notes field (prepended)\n   441→//\n   442→// IMPORTANT: Add body size limit for this endpoint — screenshots base64-encoded are 2–7MB.\n   443→// Express default JSON limit is 100KB. Add before this route:\n   444→//   app.use('/api/talent/:talentId/parse-screenshot', express.json({ limit: '10mb' }));\n   445→```\n   446→\n   447→**Implements:** Communication log UI, screenshot-to-availability parsing\n   448→\n   449→---\n   450→\n   451→## Phase 3-Deploy: Deploy Phase 3 Changes\n   452→\n   